WEBVTT

00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:16,230
Is there any problem with doing foot bath since I have a pacemaker and do the foot baths affect your electrolytes?

00:00:16,230 --> 00:00:19,230
My potassium tends to be low.

00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:30,230
If you're doing a foot bath every day, could it cause you to lose more electrolytes?

00:00:30,230 --> 00:00:34,230
Maybe a little.

00:00:34,230 --> 00:00:44,230
Would you have to be careful with if you have low potassium and you have low electrolytes and you have trouble keeping minerals in your body would be so much more than foot baths?

00:00:44,230 --> 00:00:46,230
I don't think you're really going to lose a lot.

00:00:46,230 --> 00:00:55,230
If you're using an ionic foot bath which is a little bit different than the true right foot bath, you'd have a greater chance of losing minerals using that.

00:00:55,230 --> 00:01:00,230
But still, I don't think you're losing a lot of minerals with a foot bath.

00:01:00,230 --> 00:01:05,230
If you don't, I would recommend doing foot baths every day anyhow.

00:01:05,230 --> 00:01:08,230
But I think you'd be safe doing foot baths.

